Hi Shuichiro,

The transfer and maintenance face can face south with the unit turned as show=
n. Please see the attached South-facing Transfer Interface Note Rev A.

Allow 900 mm immediately south for transfer and maintenance. The short roller=
 table must be removable so that the full 900 mm is clear when maintenance ac=
cess is needed. Separately, the east side requires at least 600 mm clear for =
isolation operation; the south work area does not replace that clearance. The=
 roller top remains FL +850 mm.

The 3,000 mm power lead can exit on the south side. Route it on that side wit=
hout crossing the north pedestrian passage. Please ask Nishimura to check the=
 actual site dimensions, floor below and fixing positions before the unit is =
fixed. This note describes the equipment interfaces; those site checks remain=
 with your team.

Best regards,
Natalie Chapman
Merecairn Equipment Ltd

On 23 July 2025 at 10:14 JST, Shuichiro Sakamoto wrote:
> Hi Natalie,
>
> Thank you for the revised envelope. In the previous orientation the new gua=
rd leaves 1,080 mm against our required 1,200 mm north walkway. We would like=
 to retain the partition and turn the unit 90 degrees counter-clockwise, keep=
ing its south-west corner at the planned position. The attached layout shows =
the resulting 1,320 mm north walkway on plan.
>
> Could you confirm whether the transfer and maintenance face can work from t=
he south with a short roller table, and what clearance is needed? We show 900=
 mm on the south side. The drawing also shows 660 mm to the fixed fence on th=
e east: please advise the width required for isolation operation there. Can t=
he power lead exit to the south, and what length is available? We want to kee=
p the north walkway clear of the lead.
>
> Please send your comments by the end of 24 July Japan time if possible. Flo=
or fixing and actual clearances still need checking on site.
>
> Best regards,
> Shuichiro Sakamoto
> Minatoryo Construction
>
> Attachment: 0723_Kaita West - South-facing layout for comment.pdf


